- op: discuss  # 2a79
  at: '2026-09-12T20:00:54Z'  # 2a79
  by: agent  # 2a79
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2a79
  clock: 6  # 2a79
  nonce: 2a79  # 2a79
  message: "SATISFIED via the canonical row INV-nihaz, PR #935 (merged 2026-09-12, dev dd50189f38). Setting the status was missed when the duplicate_of link was added, which left this reading as open — caught on a family-consistency sweep.\n\nThis items statement was: \"Commit bodies preserved via git notes must actually reach origin. They never have.\" That now holds, on its own filed measurement:\n  BEFORE  git ls-remote origin refs/notes/*        -> EMPTY\n  AFTER                                            -> refs/notes/commits present\n  BEFORE  git fetch origin refs/notes/*:refs/notes/* in a fresh clone -> nothing\n  AFTER                                            -> 728 notes\nand the merge of the fix itself printed \"Note attached to dd50189f38... and pushed\" where every prior merge printed the BLOCKED banner.\n\nBoth root causes this item named are closed: the pre-push DCO block now exempts refs/notes/*, and scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh no longer discards the push failure with 2>/dev/null || true. A regression guard in .githooks/test_hooks.sh, which CI runs, asserts the same unsigned commit blocked on refs/heads/t is allowed on refs/notes/commits."  # 2a79
